From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: misc-de <misc-de@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 07:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] network: Hidden network and hotspot in the list style

Plinius: the two Wi-Fi forms look like the other pages of Settings,
rows in a boxed list instead of labels left of the fields:

- Connect to Hidden Networks: our own page (cc-plinius-hidden-wifi.c,
  a whole file copied in prepare()) with name, security (none, WPA &
  WPA2 Personal, WPA3 Personal) and password as rows, libnma's labels
  and translations, "Connect" below the form. Interfaces that only run
  an access point are no choice. "Other Security" opens libnma's
  dialog as before, for WEP, LEAP and 802.1X.
- Wi-Fi hotspot: the explanation as the group's description, name and
  password as entry rows (generating a password from a button in the
  row), the hints below the list, "Turn On" below. The fields are
  filled when the content is realized: as a page of the window the
  dialog itself never is, so name and password stayed empty.
---
 panels/network/cc-wifi-hotspot-dialog.blp | 155 ++++++++++++------------------
 panels/network/cc-wifi-hotspot-dialog.c   |  33 +++++--
 panels/network/meson.build                |   1 +
 panels/network/network-dialogs.c          |  11 +++
 panels/network/network-dialogs.h          |   3 +
 5 files changed, 101 insertions(+), 102 deletions(-)
diff --git a/panels/network/cc-wifi-hotspot-dialog.blp b/panels/network/cc-wifi-hotspot-dialog.blp
index 038bffb5d..83f9716e2 100644
